  "id": "t02-013",
  "track": "track-02",
  "title": "API versioning OpenAPI contracts Problem Details validation pagination and idempotency",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "inventoryComplete": true,
  "concepts": [
    "An API contract is the stable agreement clients depend on: route and method semantics, request and response shapes, status codes, errors, and compatibility rules. OpenAPI describes that contract; it does not automatically make an implementation correct or backward compatible.",
    "ASP.NET Core includes OpenAPI document generation through Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi. API versioning is provided by the separate Asp.Versioning community library; distinguish its packages and APIs from framework APIs and choose URL, query, header, or media-type versioning deliberately.",
    "Problem Details gives HTTP errors a machine-readable shape. A shared writer and exception/status middleware improve consistency, but errors must still avoid leaking secrets and must preserve correct HTTP status and content negotiation behavior.",
    "Pagination is a resource contract that bounds work and defines stable continuation. Offset pagination is simple but can drift and grow costly; cursor/keyset pagination uses an ordered continuation key and behaves more predictably under writes. ASP.NET Core does not prescribe one universal pagination API.",
    "HTTP method idempotency describes intended effect under repetition. GET, HEAD, PUT, and DELETE are idempotent by HTTP semantics; POST and PATCH are not inherently so. An idempotency-key mechanism for unsafe retries is an application contract with durable deduplication and replay rules, not built-in ASP.NET Core middleware."
  ],
